<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-8">8 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Skylab 4 crew return after 84 days in space</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Gerald Carr, Edward Gibson and William Pogue splashed down after the longest crewed mission yet. Their experience of long-duration flight informed later space stations.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/moscow" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moscow.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-12">12 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet authorities arrest Aleksandr Solzhenitsyn</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Weeks after 'The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulag">Gulag</a> Archipelago' appeared in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, the Nobel laureate was arrested in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> and charged with treason. The next day he was stripped of citizenship and deported to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/carnation-revolution" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carnation-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-25">25 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Carnation Revolution topples Portugal's dictatorship</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A largely bloodless coup by army officers ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estado-novo-portugal">Estado Novo</a> regime. Democracy followed, and Portugal's African colonies gained independence within two years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carnation-revolution">Carnation Revolution</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-23">23 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Greece's military junta collapses after the Cyprus crisis</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Discredited by its coup in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> and the Turkish invasion that followed, the Greek junta handed power to civilians. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstantinos-karamanlis">Konstantinos Karamanlis</a> returned from exile the next day to restore democracy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-24">24 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Supreme Court orders Nixon to hand over the Watergate tapes</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> v. Nixon the Supreme Court ruled 8-0 that the president must surrender the tapes. Their contents destroyed his remaining support, and he resigned 16 days later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-8">8 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Richard Nixon announces his resignation</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In a televised address, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-nixon">Richard Nixon</a> said he would resign the presidency at noon the next day. Released tapes had proved his role in the Watergate cover-up, leaving him facing certain impeachment.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-9">9 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Gerald Ford becomes president after Nixon resigns</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Gerald Ford was sworn in as the 38th president, telling Americans 'our long national nightmare is over'. His pardon of Nixon a month later probably cost him the 1976 election.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-8">8 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Gerald Ford pardons Richard Nixon</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">President Ford granted Nixon a full pardon for any crimes he 'committed or may have committed' in office. Ford said it would end the national ordeal; it damaged his own popularity.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-24">24 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Fossil hunters find 'Lucy' in Ethiopia</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At Hadar, Donald Johanson and Tom Gray found the partial skeleton of a 3.2-million-year-old Australopithecus afarensis. Named Lucy, she showed that human ancestors walked upright long before brains enlarged.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-fifi" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hurricane-fifi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-fifi">Hurricane Fifi</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Hurricane Fifi was a tropical cyclone that skirted the north coast of Honduras in September 1974, bringing torrential rain that caused catastrophic flooding and landslides.</p></div></li></ol></section>
